et":true,"evidence":"JmakProtocolDecoderTest.testDecode full-message case asserts all 24 attributes (e.g. tripFuelUsed 1234.5 Double, engineLoad via KEY_ENGINE_LOAD 62.0, pto 1 Integer, gear 5 Integer, dpfRegeneration 1 Integer, wiper 2 Integer, instantFuelConsumption 18.4 Double) and passes."},{"criterion":"Fuel unit handling: 'L' or absent keeps fuel in liters; any other unit stores fuelLevel","met":true,"evidence":"Test with unit \"L\" asserts KEY_FUEL 120.5; test with no unit bit asserts KEY_FUEL 80.0; full-message test with unit \"%\" asserts KEY_FUEL_LEVEL 45.5. The first attempt failed only because my no-unit expectation was wrong (fuelLevel), which I corrected to fuel per the spec."},{"criterion":"The change is covered by tests","met":true,"evidence":"JmakProtocolDecoderTest now has 3 added verifyDecode cases covering bits 15 to 38, bit 7/8 unit routing, and the absent-unit path. Gradle: ./gradlew test --tests 'org.traccar.protocol.Jmak*' gives BUILD SUCCESSFUL, tests=1 failures=0 for JmakProtocolDecoderTest (other Jmak test classes also ran in the filtered run, 4 tests total, 0 failures)."},{"criterion":"The existing test suite still passes","met":true,"evidence":"./gradlew test --offline --rerun (JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@21): BUILD SUCCESSFUL, EXIT=0; parsed 428 XML result files: 612 tests, 27 skipped, 0 failures, 0 errors."},{"criterion":"No commit, no push, git history unchanged","met":true,"evidence":"git status shows only the two modified files (M) as working-tree changes; no git commands that change history were run."}],"human_needed":[],"harness_used":["Grep and Read to locate the JMAK decoder, its test, and Position key constants (Position.KEY_FUEL_LEVEL, KEY_ENGINE_LOAD)","ProtocolTest source inspection to confirm attribute comparison uses assertEquals on boxed values, so Integer vs Double types matter","Gradle wrapper (./gradlew test) for the filtered and full test runs"],"harness_gaps":[{"file":null,"problem":"The default `java` on thi